# What NOT to upload to Vercel.
#
# The CLI does not read .gitignore, so without this file `vercel deploy` uploads
# the working directory as it stands — which here meant 413MB and a hard failure
# on `ios/Pods/ExpoImage/SDWebImage.xcframework is not a valid symlink`. The
# native iOS build tree is generated, gitignored, irrelevant to a web export,
# and full of symlinks the archive cannot represent.
#
# Everything below is either regenerated on the build machine (node_modules via
# `npm ci`, dist via `expo export`) or has nothing to do with the web bundle.
# The web build needs src/, assets/, public/, app.json, package.json and the
# lockfile — do not add those here.

node_modules
dist
.expo
web-build

# Generated native projects. `expo export --platform web` never reads them.
ios
android

# Backend and tooling that ship nowhere near the browser.
supabase
docs
scripts/brand-fonts

.git
.github
.vscode
.claude
*.log
.DS_Store
